Senior Software Engineer - Platform
Example Corp
San Francisco, CA (Hybrid)

About Us

Example Corp is building the next generation of data infrastructure that helps engineering teams ship faster without sacrificing reliability. We are backed by top-tier investors and serve hundreds of enterprise customers worldwide.

About the Role

We are looking for a Senior Software Engineer to join our Core Platform team. You will own the design and implementation of critical backend systems that power our real-time data pipeline and developer-facing APIs. This is a high-impact role where you will work closely with product, design, and infrastructure teams to define and build the technical foundation of our platform.

What You Will Do

- Design, build, and operate scalable backend services and APIs that process millions of events per day.
- Lead architectural decisions for distributed systems, balancing performance, reliability, and developer experience.
- Own end-to-end delivery of major platform features from RFC through production rollout.
- Mentor junior engineers and raise the technical bar through code reviews, design docs, and incident response.
- Collaborate with cross-functional teams to define system requirements and integration patterns.
- Drive improvements in observability, testing, and deployment automation across the platform.

What We Are Looking For

- 5+ years of professional software engineering experience, with at least 2 years working on distributed backend systems at scale.
- Strong proficiency in Python or Go, with experience building production-grade services and REST APIs.
- Deep understanding of distributed systems concepts including consensus, replication, eventual consistency, and failure modes.
- Experience with cloud infrastructure (AWS or GCP), Kubernetes, and infrastructure-as-code tools like Terraform.
- Hands-on experience with message brokers such as Kafka, RabbitMQ, or SQS.
- Familiarity with relational and NoSQL databases (PostgreSQL, MongoDB, Redis) and query optimization.
- Experience with observability tools (Datadog, Prometheus, Grafana) and production incident management.
- Strong communication skills and ability to lead technical discussions across teams.

Nice to Have

- Experience with real-time stream processing frameworks (Spark Streaming, Flink).
- Background in platform engineering or developer experience tooling.
- Contributions to open-source projects or public technical writing.
- Experience with ML model serving infrastructure or feature stores.

Benefits

- Competitive salary ($180,000 - $240,000) plus equity.
- Comprehensive health, dental, and vision insurance.
- 401(k) with company match.
- Flexible PTO and remote work options.
- Annual learning and development stipend.
- Home office setup allowance.
